      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GLENEAGLE RULER (6) was good when he chased a handy one for second in a higher-graded race at Bathurst last start and had come from the back row for a win when resuming at that venue three back. Race fit and looks to have found a suitable assignment. MAJOR BYE (1) is another that beat some capable rivals when successful at his most recent outing by 1.2 metres in a nice return to form at Newcastle. Has the speed to take advantage of the inside draw. ETHANS REVENGE (5) wasn't too far from the placings in his three outings during the Breeders Challenge series. Went into that off a win at this circuit and distance. Contender. UPTOWN CHANCE (3) had a horror draw in a Breeders Challenge semi-final last start but had led to win a heat prior so is much better served by this barrier. ROCKNROLL COWBOY (10) draws wide but was better last week and strikes at 50 per cent at this circuit and distance.",
